    "emissionFsharp": "open Fuaran.UI.OpStream\n\n// Freeze: tree + Binding.State (+ optional bounded op-history + chain head for\n// integrity), canonical-encode → deflate → base64url. Deterministic bytes.\nlet bundle = Teleport.encode { Tree = tree; State = stateMap\n                               History = Bounded lastN; ChainHead = head }\n\n// Carry: URL fragment (nothing touches a server) or QR of the same string.\n// Resume (receiving side): decode → PreEmitValidate → the FGP 3 gate\n// (wire-survivable actions dispatch; anything closure-shaped was never encodable)\n// → state re-seated by stable NodeId.\nlet resumed = Teleport.decodeValidateResume bundleString",
    "variantPoints": "| Slot | Type | AI substitution behaviour |\n|---|---|---|\n| payload | tree+state / +history | default tree+state; \"with the history / how we got here\" → include the bounded op-history if the size budget allows, else truncate history first, never state |\n| carrier | link vs QR | \"link / send\" → fragment URL; \"phone / scan\" → QR; same string either way |\n| persistence | one-shot vs local resume | \"come back tomorrow\" (same device) → localStorage variant; cross-device → fragment/QR |",
    "antiPatterns": "- **Trying to teleport closures.** Anything closure-shaped was never on the wire; if an app leans\n  on host-side `Custom` behaviour, the bundle carries the reference, not the behaviour — the\n  receiving host must have the same registrations. Say so rather than silently degrading.\n- **State via screenshot-of-JSON.** Re-emitting a \"similar\" tree with values pasted into props is\n  an approximation that breaks bindings; the bundle is the mechanism.\n- **Unbounded history in the bundle.** The fragment/QR ceiling is real (#109 hit it); truncate\n  history first, state never — and surface the truncation.\n- **Teleporting secrets.** The bundle is as public as the channel it rides; state containing\n  credentials/PII needs the same handling as any export — flag, don't assume.\n- **Skipping the gate on resume.** The receive path is decode → validate → gate, identical to any\n  other wire ingress; a \"trusted because we made it\" bypass reintroduces the class FGP 3 closed."
